      "id": "pf_56906436_value",
      "label": "Text — Value",
      "default": "<span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">INSTALLATION</span>: Kessick Wine Storage Systems, LLC (“Kessick”)\rdirects you our customer (“Customer”) to the Installation\rGuide and Installation Video included on our website\r(www.wineasaert.com) for your new Kessick <span style=\"font-style: italic;\">WinePanel</span>™\rSystem or <span style=\"font-style: italic;\">WineWall</span>™ System. The Installation Guide and\rInstallation Video are for informational use only and shall not\rbe regarded as a warranty. It is imperative that the installer\rof your new Kessick Wine Panel System or Wine Wall System\rreview and understand the specifications and logistics\runique to the Customer’s chosen location for installation, as\rwell as the written instructions in the Installation Guide and\rthe Installation Video prior to beginning installation. It is the\rresponsibility of the installer to understand the installation\rinstructions contained within the Installation Guide and\rInstallation Video, or to obtain clarification of the installation\rinstructions, prior to beginning the installation process, and\rto follow all applicable local building codes.\r<br><br>The Wine Panel System and Wine Wall System have been\rdesigned and engineered to securely fasten a back-panel to a\r<span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">wood framed structural wall</span> (gypsum board over wood 2x4,\rtypical) and to support the weight of the finished panel with\rthe Kessick-supplied wine bottle hardware and a “live load” of\rwine bottles, at a maximum weight of 3lbs per wine bottle."
