      "type": "html",
      "id": "pf_ae0b80a8_value",
      "label": "Text — Value",
      "default": "<span style=\"font-style: italic;\">Kessick LLC is committed to high quality products and great customer service. It is our desire to have satisfied\ncustomers that enjoy their Kessick wine storage system and are pleased with the aesthetics and function as well\nas the installation process. Kessick Wine As Art products have been designed and engineered to enable the best\npossible customer experience.</span>"
    },
    {
      "type": "html",
      "id": "pf_b4563739_value",
      "label": "Text — Value",
      "default": "<span style=\"font-style: italic;\">WineWall</span>™ System: The Wine Panel back-panel should\rbe installed directly into a vertical wall surface with the\rKessick-supplied wood screws into a wood framing\rstructure. The Wine Wall System requires a minimum\rof 3 wood screws for every 14” x 14” area (i.e., 42”x\r42” – 18 wood screws into wall studs). <span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">*Hollow wall\ranchors are not acceptable fasteners for installation\rof the Wine Wall System and are NOT TO BE USED\rin installation of the Wine Wall System. Metal wall\rstuds are not suitable for installation unless sheathed\rwith  ” –  ” plywood.</span> * Kessick strongly advises the\rCustomer to engage a licensed professional to install\rthe Wine Wall System into any non-wood framed (i.e.,\rmasonry, brick, block, concrete, stone) structures.<br><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">WARNING: IMPROPER INSTALLATION OF THE\rWINE WALL SYSTEM (INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED\rTO THE USE OF HOLLOW WALL ANCHORS, OR\rMETAL WALL STUDS UNSHEATHED TO  ” –  ”\rPLYWOOD, OR FAILURE TO FOLLOW THE\rINSTALLATION GUIDE OR INSTALLATION VIDEO)\rMAY RESULT IN SERIOUS PERSONAL INJURY.\rINSTALLATION OF THE WINE WALL SYSTEM\rINTO ANY STRUCTURE OTHER THAN WOODFRAMING,\rINCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO\rMASONRY, BRICK, BLOCK, CONCRETE, OR\rSTONE, SHOULD BE PERFORMED BY A LICENSED\rPROFESSIONAL ONLY.</span>"
